% Test cases for the suction pumps policy (suction_pumps.le): synthetic
% claims, one or two per criterion of LCD L33612 and per payment condition
% of dmepos.le and Policy Article A52519. Findings are recorded as the
% treating practitioner's or the Council's; a finding nobody made leaves the
% answer conditional. The queries: whether the claim is payable (the first
% query, so "stage" reads its checklist), whether it is reasonable and
% necessary, and what minimal change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base suction_pumps cases includes these resources:
    suction_pumps.

the knowledge base suction_pumps cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete first-month claim for a respiratory suction pump (E0600): a
% tracheostomy, the treating practitioner's finding on the secretions, the
% diagnosis code on the claim, and every documentation requirement in the
% record. E0600 is not on the CMS face-to-face list: the order need only
% reach the supplier before the date of service.
scenario respiratory_pump_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the suction pump.
    the HCPCS code of the suction pump is "E0600".
    the suction pump is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Ann documents tracheostomy.
    the finding difficulty clearing secretions about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "thick secretions through the tracheostomy tube after a laryngectomy, needing suction several times a day".
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "Z93.0".
    the order for the suction pump is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the suction pump is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the suction pump includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the suction pump includes order date.
    the order for the suction pump includes description of the item.
    the order for the suction pump includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the suction pump includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the suction pump was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the suction pump was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the suction pump.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The finding without a condition of the LCD's list: chronic bronchitis is
% not one of them.
scenario respiratory_pump_other_condition is:
    claim 1 is for the suction pump.
    the HCPCS code of the suction pump is "E0600".
    the suction pump is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Ben documents chronic bronchitis.
    the finding difficulty clearing secretions about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% A gastric suction pump (E2000) on the treating practitioner's finding;
% and one the Council finds unsupported.
scenario gastric_pump is:
    claim 1 is for the gastric pump.
    the HCPCS code of the gastric pump is "E2000".
    the gastric pump is furnished to Cy.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding unable to empty gastric secretions about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "gastric outlet obstruction from an inoperable carcinoma of the pancreas, decompressed through a gastrostomy tube".
    claim 2 is for the second gastric pump.
    the HCPCS code of the second gastric pump is "E2000".
    the second gastric pump is furnished to Dee.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the finding unable to empty gastric secretions about Dee is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the record shows a nasogastric tube for one week of postoperative ileus, resolved before discharge, and no continuing inability to empty the stomach".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Tracheal catheters with Ann's covered pump used for tracheostomy
% suctioning: 60 catheters for 30 days (at most 3 a day) are within the
% limit; 120 are not; a closed system catheter (A4605) without a covered
% ventilator is not covered; with one it is.
scenario tracheal_catheters is:
    claim 1 is for the catheters.
    the HCPCS code of the catheters is "A4624".
    the catheters is furnished to Ann.
    the catheters is an accessory of the suction pump.
    claim 1 covers 30 days.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 60.
    claim 2 is for the extra catheters.
    the HCPCS code of the extra catheters is "A4624".
    the extra catheters is furnished to Ann.
    the extra catheters is an accessory of the suction pump.
    claim 2 covers 30 days.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 120.
    claim 3 is for the closed system catheters.
    the HCPCS code of the closed system catheters is "A4605".
    the closed system catheters is furnished to Ann.
    the closed system catheters is an accessory of the suction pump.
    claim 4 is for the ventilator catheters.
    the HCPCS code of the ventilator catheters is "A4605".
    the ventilator catheters is furnished to Eve.
    the ventilator catheters is an accessory of the second suction pump.
    the HCPCS code of the suction pump is "E0600".
    the suction pump is furnished to Ann.
    the suction pump is used for tracheostomy suctioning.
    the medical record of Ann documents tracheostomy.
    the finding difficulty clearing secretions about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the HCPCS code of the second suction pump is "E0600".
    the second suction pump is furnished to Eve.
    the second suction pump is used for tracheostomy suctioning.
    the medical record of Eve documents tracheostomy.
    the finding difficulty clearing secretions about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    Eve requires the use of a covered ventilator.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 4 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Oropharyngeal suctioning for Fay, unconscious after a stroke, with a
% covered pump: 12 catheters (A4628) for 28 days (at most 3 a week) are
% within the limit; 13 are not; saline (A4216) for oropharyngeal suctioning
% is not covered; saline used to clear a catheter after tracheostomy
% suctioning of Ann is.
scenario oropharyngeal_suctioning is:
    claim 1 is for the oral catheters.
    the HCPCS code of the oral catheters is "A4628".
    the oral catheters is furnished to Fay.
    the oral catheters is an accessory of the suction pump.
    the oral catheters is used for suctioning in the oropharynx.
    claim 1 covers 28 days.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 12.
    claim 2 is for the extra oral catheters.
    the HCPCS code of the extra oral catheters is "A4628".
    the extra oral catheters is furnished to Fay.
    the extra oral catheters is an accessory of the suction pump.
    the extra oral catheters is used for suctioning in the oropharynx.
    claim 2 covers 28 days.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 13.
    claim 3 is for the saline.
    the HCPCS code of the saline is "A4216".
    the saline is furnished to Fay.
    the saline is an accessory of the suction pump.
    claim 4 is for the tracheostomy saline.
    the HCPCS code of the tracheostomy saline is "A4216".
    the tracheostomy saline is furnished to Ann.
    the tracheostomy saline is an accessory of the second suction pump.
    the tracheostomy saline is used to clear a suction catheter after tracheostomy suctioning.
    the HCPCS code of the suction pump is "E0600".
    the suction pump is furnished to Fay.
    the medical record of Fay documents unconsciousness.
    the finding difficulty clearing secretions about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the HCPCS code of the second suction pump is "E0600".
    the second suction pump is furnished to Ann.
    the second suction pump is used for tracheostomy suctioning.
    the medical record of Ann documents tracheostomy.
    the finding difficulty clearing secretions about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 4 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Tracheal catheters with their documentation, but the claim carries the
% code of the laryngeal cancer (C32.9), not the tracheostomy status code
% the Policy Article requires: reasonable and necessary, not payable.
scenario catheters_without_tracheostomy_code is:
    claim 1 is for the catheters.
    the HCPCS code of the catheters is "A4624".
    the catheters is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the catheters is an accessory of the suction pump.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-01.
    claim 1 covers 30 days.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 60.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "C32.9".
    the HCPCS code of the suction pump is "E0600".
    the suction pump is furnished to Ann.
    the suction pump is used for tracheostomy suctioning.
    the medical record of Ann documents tracheostomy.
    the finding difficulty clearing secretions about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the catheters is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the catheters is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the catheters includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the catheters includes order date.
    the order for the catheters includes description of the item.
    the order for the catheters includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the catheters includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the catheters was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the catheters was delivered on 2026-04-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the catheters.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].

% Reasonable and necessary, but no proof of delivery: payable fails at the
% remedy, and the flip adds the missing proof.
scenario no_proof_of_delivery is:
    claim 1 is for the suction pump.
    the HCPCS code of the suction pump is "E0600".
    the suction pump is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Ann documents tracheostomy.
    the finding difficulty clearing secretions about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "Z93.0".
    the order for the suction pump is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the suction pump is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the suction pump includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the suction pump includes order date.
    the order for the suction pump includes description of the item.
    the order for the suction pump includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the suction pump includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the suction pump was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the suction pump was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the supplier holds proof of delivery for the suction pump"]].

% Wound suction: a wound suction pump (K0743) and its dressing set (K0745)
% are never covered; a disposable device (A9272) is outside the benefit.
scenario wound_suction is:
    claim 1 is for the wound pump.
    the HCPCS code of the wound pump is "K0743".
    the wound pump is furnished to Gus.
    the residence of Gus is private residence.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    claim 2 is for the dressing set.
    the HCPCS code of the dressing set is "K0745".
    the dressing set is furnished to Gus.
    the dressing set is an accessory of the wound pump.
    claim 3 is for the disposable device.
    the HCPCS code of the disposable device is "A9272".
    the disposable device is furnished to Gus.
    rn expects answers [].
    pay expects answers [].
